{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>And doing kindness to thousands.</b> And it is written: \"to a thousand generations\" (Deuteronomy 7:9). People will suppose this is a contradiction, but it is not so, for it is written: \"If you keep My commandments, HaShem will keep for you the covenant and the kindness which He swore to your fathers\" — they are the three patriarchs — and this is: \"who keeps the covenant and the kindness to those who love Him and to those who keep His commandments, to a thousand generations\" (ibid.). And in this pericope He said something else: \"and doing kindness to thousands,\" the meaning being without end, for ever and ever. This matter is interpreted in two ways: the first, that HaShem does kindness to those who love Him so that their souls stand forever, for thousands of thousands of generations; the second, that HaShem does good to their children, who are like them, without end. Thus David said: \"But the kindness of HaShem is from everlasting to everlasting upon those who fear Him, and His righteousness to children's children\" (Psalms 103:17). Now there is no doubt that HaShem's kindness is eternal upon those who fear Him; but because He mentioned \"children's children,\" in the manner of \"and His righteousness stands forever\" (Psalms 111:3), it was necessary to specify whether the children are good, therefore He said afterward: \"to those who keep His covenant.\" In the pericope of כי תשא I shall explain to you how the attribute of visiting the iniquity of fathers enters into the attribute of mercy:" "<b>And the word \"to those who love.\"</b> They are the devout, and \"to those who keep His commandments\" are the righteous:"], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {0 "The closing colon (:) appears in the source; it points forward to the promised discussion in the כי תשא pericope (Exodus 34:6–7)."}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:36:11.725189978Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}